<title>TURKEY: Turk Yapi Kredi Bank 96 profit up 40 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Yapi Kredi Bank 96 profit up 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Dec 1996 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	 881.49   vs   1,951.11</p>
<p>    Net profit		     22,724.43   vs  16,225.43</p>
<p>    Net interest income	  35,284.28   vs  10,125.41</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense    8,806.95   vs   7,665.80</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans	675.27   vs     515.72</p>
<p>    Loans			   295,762.67   vs 129,128.17</p>
<p>    Deposits			420,679.12   vs 188,558.34</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed		 27,272.40   vs   6,298.08</p>
<p>    Equity			   42,777.92   vs  17,760.55</p>
<p>    Capital			  25,779.60   vs   8,316.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Yapi Kredi Bankasi A.S., a leading Turkish commercial bank, is largely owned by financial and industrial group Cukurova.</p>
<p>The bank plans to pay out a 740 lira dividend per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share, including 600 lira in cash and 140 lira in the form of bonus share after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on March 31.</p>
<p>Figures above do not take into consideration Turkey's 84.9 percent 1996 wholesale inflation.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
